## 에러 처리 패턴

### Java 17 + Exception Handling
```java
// ✅ Sealed Interface for Results (Java 17)
public sealed interface ProcessingResult 
    permits ProcessingResult.Success, ProcessingResult.Error {
    
    record Success(String eventId, Instant processedAt) implements ProcessingResult {}
    record Error(String eventId, String error, Throwable cause) implements ProcessingResult {}
    
    // Pattern matching helper
    static <T> T handle(ProcessingResult result, 
                       Function<Success, T> onSuccess,
                       Function<Error, T> onError) {
        return switch (result) {
            case Success success -> onSuccess.apply(success);
            case Error error -> onError.apply(error);
        };
    }
}
```

### Kotlin Error Handling
```kotlin
// ✅ Result 타입 활용
sealed class EventResult<out T> {
    data class Success<T>(val value: T) : EventResult<T>()
    data class Error(val error: String, val cause: Throwable? = null) : EventResult<Nothing>()
    
    inline fun <U> map(transform: (T) -> U): EventResult<U> = when (this) {
        is Success -> Success(transform(value))
        is Error -> this
    }
    
    inline fun onSuccess(action: (T) -> Unit): EventResult<T> = also {
        if (this is Success) action(value)
    }
    
    inline fun onError(action: (String, Throwable?) -> Unit): EventResult<T> = also {
        if (this is Error) action(error, cause)
    }
}

// 사용
fun processEvent(event: UserEvent): EventResult<ProcessedEvent> = try {
    val processed = transformEvent(event)
    EventResult.Success(processed)
} catch (e: Exception) {
    EventResult.Error("Processing failed for ${event.userId}", e)
}
```

## 로깅 & 모니터링

### Structured Logging
```java
// ✅ Logback + Structured Logging
@Slf4j
@Component
public class EventProcessor {
    
    public void processEvent(UserEvent event) {
        // MDC for correlation
        try (MDCCloseable mdc = MDC.putCloseable("eventId", event.eventId())) {
            log.info("Processing event: userId={}, type={}, timestamp={}", 
                event.userId(), event.eventType(), event.timestamp());
                
            // Processing logic
            var result = transform(event);
            
            log.info("Event processed successfully: duration={}ms", 
                Duration.between(event.timestamp(), Instant.now()).toMillis());
        } catch (Exception e) {
            log.error("Event processing failed: userId={}, error={}", 
                event.userId(), e.getMessage(), e);
        }
    }
}
```

### Micrometer Metrics
```kotlin
// ✅ 커스텀 메트릭
@Component
class StreamsMetrics(private val meterRegistry: MeterRegistry) {
    
    private val eventCounter = Counter.builder("streams.events.processed")
        .description("Number of events processed")
        .register(meterRegistry)
        
    private val processingTimer = Timer.builder("streams.events.processing.duration")
        .description("Event processing duration")
        .register(meterRegistry)
    
    fun recordEventProcessed(eventType: String) {
        eventCounter.increment(Tags.of("type", eventType))
    }
    
    fun <T> timeProcessing(operation: () -> T): T {
        return processingTimer.recordCallable(operation)!!
    }
}
```

## 테스팅 패턴

### Java 17 + JUnit 5
```java
// ✅ 파라미터화 테스트 + Records
@ParameterizedTest
@MethodSource("eventTestCases")
void shouldProcessEvents(EventTestCase testCase) {
    // Given
    var event = testCase.inputEvent();
    
    // When
    var result = processor.process(event);
    
    // Then
    switch (result) {
        case ProcessingResult.Success(var eventId, var processedAt) -> {
            assertThat(eventId).isEqualTo(event.eventId());
            assertThat(processedAt).isAfter(event.timestamp());
        }
        case ProcessingResult.Error(var eventId, var error, var cause) -> {
            fail("Expected success but got error: " + error);
        }
    }
}

static Stream<EventTestCase> eventTestCases() {
    return Stream.of(
        new EventTestCase("valid event", createValidEvent(), true),
        new EventTestCase("invalid event", createInvalidEvent(), false)
    );
}

record EventTestCase(String description, UserEvent inputEvent, boolean expectSuccess) {}
```

### Kotlin Testing
```kotlin
// ✅ Kotest 스타일
class EventProcessorTest : StringSpec({
    
    "should process valid events successfully" {
        val event = UserEvent(
            eventId = "test-1",
            userId = "user-123",
            eventType = "REGISTRATION",
            timestamp = Instant.now(),
            properties = mapOf("email" to "test@example.com")
        )
        
        val result = processor.process(event)
        
        result shouldBe EventResult.Success::class
        (result as EventResult.Success).value.userId shouldBe event.userId
    }
    
    "should handle processing errors gracefully" {
        val invalidEvent = UserEvent(
            eventId = "test-2",
            userId = "", // Invalid
            eventType = "REGISTRATION",
            timestamp = Instant.now(),
            properties = emptyMap()
        )
        
        val result = processor.process(invalidEvent)
        
        result shouldBe EventResult.Error::class
        (result as EventResult.Error).error shouldContain "validation failed"
    }
})
```

## 상호운용성 가이드

### Java에서 Kotlin 호출
```java
// ✅ Kotlin 확장 함수는 static 메서드로 호출
import static com.example.extensions.StreamExtensionsKt.*;

public class JavaProcessor {
    public void processStream(KStream<String, UserEvent> stream) {
        // Kotlin extension function 호출
        var filtered = filterNotNull(stream);
        var logged = logProcessing(filtered, "java-processor");
    }
}
```

### Kotlin에서 Java 호출
```kotlin
// ✅ Java records를 자연스럽게 사용
class KotlinProcessor(private val javaService: JavaEventService) {
    
    fun processEvent(event: UserEvent): ProcessingResult {
        return javaService.process(event).let { result ->
            when (result) {
                is ProcessingResult.Success -> {
                    log.info("Success: ${result.eventId}")
                    result
                }
                is ProcessingResult.Error -> {
                    log.error("Error: ${result.error}", result.cause)
                    result
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```